      timeline: [
        'Late 18th century: Game likely developed in Austria.',
        '1806: Tarocktappen mentioned in Viennese comic opera and letters.',
        '1821: First printed rules in Vienna.',
        '19th–20th century: Played in Germany and Austria; four-player variants such as Königrufen developed.',
      ],
      evolution: 'Originally had Tapper, Dreier, Solo bids; Tapper (use all six talon cards) was soon dropped. Modern bidding has Dreier, Unterer, Oberer, Solo with optional announcements (win last trick with Trump I, or Valat).',
      cultural: 'Was the preferred card game of Viennese coffee houses before the Anschluss; still played sporadically. Considered a good introduction to Tarock before Cego, Illustrated Tarock, or Königrufen.',
